{
  "title": "Boss: the sales cube",
  "summary": "Join three tables safely, then summarise, share out and pivot the result.",
  "minutes": 10,
  "kind": "boss",
  "steps": [
    {
      "type": "learn",
      "title": "Three tables",
      "body": "You have `orders` (`order_id`, `customer_id`, `sku`, `qty`, `month`), `customers` (`customer_id`, `region`) and `products` (`sku`, `price`, `updated`, where a product **can appear more than once** after a price change). Build the joined table without losing or duplicating orders, then answer the questions a sales manager asks.\n\nThe tests use these tables:\n\n```python\norders = pd.DataFrame({\n    \"order_id\": [1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7, 8],\n    \"customer_id\": [10, 20, 10, 30, 20, 10, 40, 30],\n    \"sku\": [\"T1\", \"C1\", \"C1\", \"T1\", \"T1\", \"C1\", \"T1\", \"C1\"],\n    \"qty\": [2, 1, 3, 1, 4, 1, 2, 2],\n    \"month\": [\"Jan\", \"Jan\", \"Feb\", \"Feb\", \"Feb\", \"Mar\", \"Mar\", \"Mar\"],\n})\ncustomers = pd.DataFrame({\"customer_id\": [10, 20, 30, 40],\n                          \"region\": [\"North\", \"South\", \"North\", \"East\"]})\nproducts = pd.DataFrame({\"sku\": [\"T1\", \"C1\", \"T1\"], \"price\": [3.0, 8.0, 3.5],\n                         \"updated\": [\"2024-01-01\", \"2024-01-01\", \"2024-06-01\"]})\n```\n\nSo `T1` costs 3.5 (its latest price) and `C1` costs 8.0."
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "title": "Enrich the orders",
      "prompt": "Write `enrich(orders, customers, products)` that returns one row per order with `region`, `price` (the **latest** price for the sku) and `revenue = qty * price`. Use left joins with `validate=\"many_to_one\"`. Keep the original order of the orders.",
      "starter": "import pandas as pd\n\n\ndef enrich(orders, customers, products):\n    pass\n",
      "solution": [
        "import pandas as pd",
        "",
        "",
        "def enrich(orders, customers, products):",
        "    latest = products.sort_values(\"updated\").drop_duplicates(\"sku\", keep=\"last\")",
        "    m = orders.merge(customers, on=\"customer_id\", how=\"left\", validate=\"many_to_one\")",
        "    m = m.merge(latest[[\"sku\", \"price\"]], on=\"sku\", how=\"left\", validate=\"many_to_one\")",
        "    m[\"revenue\"] = m[\"qty\"] * m[\"price\"]",
        "    return m"
      ],
      "hints": [
        "De-duplicate products first (latest `updated` wins).",
        "Two merges in a row: customers, then products."
      ],
      "template": [
        "{{CODE}}",
        "",
        "_orders = pd.DataFrame({",
        "    \"order_id\": [1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7, 8],",
        "    \"customer_id\": [10, 20, 10, 30, 20, 10, 40, 30],",
        "    \"sku\": [\"T1\", \"C1\", \"C1\", \"T1\", \"T1\", \"C1\", \"T1\", \"C1\"],",
        "    \"qty\": [2, 1, 3, 1, 4, 1, 2, 2],",
        "    \"month\": [\"Jan\", \"Jan\", \"Feb\", \"Feb\", \"Feb\", \"Mar\", \"Mar\", \"Mar\"],",
        "})",
        "_customers = pd.DataFrame({\"customer_id\": [10, 20, 30, 40], \"region\": [\"North\", \"South\", \"North\", \"East\"]})",
        "_products = pd.DataFrame({\"sku\": [\"T1\", \"C1\", \"T1\"], \"price\": [3.0, 8.0, 3.5],",
        "                          \"updated\": [\"2024-01-01\", \"2024-01-01\", \"2024-06-01\"]})",
        "",
        "_m = enrich(_orders, _customers, _products)",
        "Dojo.eq(\"one row per order\", list(range(1, 9)), _m[\"order_id\"].tolist())",
        "Dojo.eq(\"regions\", [\"North\", \"South\", \"North\", \"North\", \"South\", \"North\", \"East\", \"North\"], _m[\"region\"].tolist())",
        "Dojo.eq(\"latest prices\", [3.5, 8.0, 8.0, 3.5, 3.5, 8.0, 3.5, 8.0], _m[\"price\"].tolist())",
        "Dojo.eq(\"revenue\", [7.0, 8.0, 24.0, 3.5, 14.0, 8.0, 7.0, 16.0], _m[\"revenue\"].tolist())"
      ],
      "require": [
        {
          "pattern": "validate",
          "message": "Validates the merges"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "title": "Region summary",
      "prompt": "Your `enrich` is in the editor. Write `region_summary(m)` for its output. Return a DataFrame with columns `region`, `revenue` (sum), `orders` (count of orders), `customers` (number of **different** customers), sorted by `revenue` descending with a fresh index.",
      "starter": "import pandas as pd\n\n\ndef enrich(orders, customers, products):\n    latest = products.sort_values(\"updated\").drop_duplicates(\"sku\", keep=\"last\")\n    m = orders.merge(customers, on=\"customer_id\", how=\"left\", validate=\"many_to_one\")\n    m = m.merge(latest[[\"sku\", \"price\"]], on=\"sku\", how=\"left\", validate=\"many_to_one\")\n    m[\"revenue\"] = m[\"qty\"] * m[\"price\"]\n    return m\n\n\ndef region_summary(m):\n    pass\n",
      "solution": [
        "import pandas as pd",
        "",
        "",
        "def enrich(orders, customers, products):",
        "    latest = products.sort_values(\"updated\").drop_duplicates(\"sku\", keep=\"last\")",
        "    m = orders.merge(customers, on=\"customer_id\", how=\"left\", validate=\"many_to_one\")",
        "    m = m.merge(latest[[\"sku\", \"price\"]], on=\"sku\", how=\"left\", validate=\"many_to_one\")",
        "    m[\"revenue\"] = m[\"qty\"] * m[\"price\"]",
        "    return m",
        "",
        "",
        "def region_summary(m):",
        "    out = m.groupby(\"region\", as_index=False).agg(",
        "        revenue=(\"revenue\", \"sum\"),",
        "        orders=(\"order_id\", \"count\"),",
        "        customers=(\"customer_id\", \"nunique\"),",
        "    )",
        "    return out.sort_values(\"revenue\", ascending=False).reset_index(drop=True)"
      ],
      "hints": [
        "Named aggregation with `\"nunique\"` for customers."
      ],
      "template": [
        "{{CODE}}",
        "",
        "_orders = pd.DataFrame({",
        "    \"order_id\": [1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7, 8],",
        "    \"customer_id\": [10, 20, 10, 30, 20, 10, 40, 30],",
        "    \"sku\": [\"T1\", \"C1\", \"C1\", \"T1\", \"T1\", \"C1\", \"T1\", \"C1\"],",
        "    \"qty\": [2, 1, 3, 1, 4, 1, 2, 2],",
        "    \"month\": [\"Jan\", \"Jan\", \"Feb\", \"Feb\", \"Feb\", \"Mar\", \"Mar\", \"Mar\"],",
        "})",
        "_customers = pd.DataFrame({\"customer_id\": [10, 20, 30, 40], \"region\": [\"North\", \"South\", \"North\", \"East\"]})",
        "_products = pd.DataFrame({\"sku\": [\"T1\", \"C1\", \"T1\"], \"price\": [3.0, 8.0, 3.5],",
        "                          \"updated\": [\"2024-01-01\", \"2024-01-01\", \"2024-06-01\"]})",
        "",
        "_r = region_summary(enrich(_orders, _customers, _products))",
        "Dojo.eq(\"columns\", [\"region\", \"revenue\", \"orders\", \"customers\"], list(_r.columns))",
        "Dojo.eq(\"regions by revenue\", [\"North\", \"South\", \"East\"], _r[\"region\"].tolist())",
        "Dojo.eq(\"revenue\", [58.5, 22.0, 7.0], _r[\"revenue\"].tolist())",
        "Dojo.eq(\"orders\", [5, 2, 1], _r[\"orders\"].tolist())",
        "Dojo.eq(\"different customers\", [2, 1, 1], _r[\"customers\"].tolist())"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "title": "Customer share of region",
      "prompt": "Write `customer_shares(m)` for the output of `enrich`. Return a DataFrame with one row per (`region`, `customer_id`), the columns `region`, `customer_id`, `revenue` (that customer's total) and `share` (that total divided by the region's total, rounded to 2 decimals), sorted by `region` then `customer_id`, fresh index.",
      "starter": "import pandas as pd\n\n\ndef enrich(orders, customers, products):\n    latest = products.sort_values(\"updated\").drop_duplicates(\"sku\", keep=\"last\")\n    m = orders.merge(customers, on=\"customer_id\", how=\"left\", validate=\"many_to_one\")\n    m = m.merge(latest[[\"sku\", \"price\"]], on=\"sku\", how=\"left\", validate=\"many_to_one\")\n    m[\"revenue\"] = m[\"qty\"] * m[\"price\"]\n    return m\n\n\ndef customer_shares(m):\n    pass\n",
      "solution": [
        "import pandas as pd",
        "",
        "",
        "def enrich(orders, customers, products):",
        "    latest = products.sort_values(\"updated\").drop_duplicates(\"sku\", keep=\"last\")",
        "    m = orders.merge(customers, on=\"customer_id\", how=\"left\", validate=\"many_to_one\")",
        "    m = m.merge(latest[[\"sku\", \"price\"]], on=\"sku\", how=\"left\", validate=\"many_to_one\")",
        "    m[\"revenue\"] = m[\"qty\"] * m[\"price\"]",
        "    return m",
        "",
        "",
        "def customer_shares(m):",
        "    per = m.groupby([\"region\", \"customer_id\"], as_index=False)[\"revenue\"].sum()",
        "    per[\"share\"] = (per[\"revenue\"] / per.groupby(\"region\")[\"revenue\"].transform(\"sum\")).round(2)",
        "    return per.sort_values([\"region\", \"customer_id\"]).reset_index(drop=True)"
      ],
      "hints": [
        "Aggregate to one row per region and customer first.",
        "Then divide by `per.groupby(\"region\")[\"revenue\"].transform(\"sum\")`."
      ],
      "template": [
        "{{CODE}}",
        "",
        "_orders = pd.DataFrame({",
        "    \"order_id\": [1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7, 8],",
        "    \"customer_id\": [10, 20, 10, 30, 20, 10, 40, 30],",
        "    \"sku\": [\"T1\", \"C1\", \"C1\", \"T1\", \"T1\", \"C1\", \"T1\", \"C1\"],",
        "    \"qty\": [2, 1, 3, 1, 4, 1, 2, 2],",
        "    \"month\": [\"Jan\", \"Jan\", \"Feb\", \"Feb\", \"Feb\", \"Mar\", \"Mar\", \"Mar\"],",
        "})",
        "_customers = pd.DataFrame({\"customer_id\": [10, 20, 30, 40], \"region\": [\"North\", \"South\", \"North\", \"East\"]})",
        "_products = pd.DataFrame({\"sku\": [\"T1\", \"C1\", \"T1\"], \"price\": [3.0, 8.0, 3.5],",
        "                          \"updated\": [\"2024-01-01\", \"2024-01-01\", \"2024-06-01\"]})",
        "",
        "_c = customer_shares(enrich(_orders, _customers, _products))",
        "Dojo.eq(\"columns\", [\"region\", \"customer_id\", \"revenue\", \"share\"], list(_c.columns))",
        "Dojo.eq(\"regions\", [\"East\", \"North\", \"North\", \"South\"], _c[\"region\"].tolist())",
        "Dojo.eq(\"customers\", [40, 10, 30, 20], _c[\"customer_id\"].tolist())",
        "Dojo.eq(\"revenue\", [7.0, 39.0, 19.5, 22.0], _c[\"revenue\"].tolist())",
        "Dojo.eq(\"shares\", [1.0, 0.67, 0.33, 1.0], _c[\"share\"].tolist())"
      ],
      "require": [
        {
          "pattern": "transform",
          "message": "Uses transform for the region total"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "title": "The month by region grid",
      "prompt": "Write `month_grid(m)` for the output of `enrich`: summed revenue with regions as rows and months as columns **in the order `Jan`, `Feb`, `Mar`**, `0` where there were no sales, plus a final column `growth` = `Mar` minus `Jan`.",
      "starter": "import pandas as pd\n\n\ndef enrich(orders, customers, products):\n    latest = products.sort_values(\"updated\").drop_duplicates(\"sku\", keep=\"last\")\n    m = orders.merge(customers, on=\"customer_id\", how=\"left\", validate=\"many_to_one\")\n    m = m.merge(latest[[\"sku\", \"price\"]], on=\"sku\", how=\"left\", validate=\"many_to_one\")\n    m[\"revenue\"] = m[\"qty\"] * m[\"price\"]\n    return m\n\n\ndef month_grid(m):\n    pass\n",
      "solution": [
        "import pandas as pd",
        "",
        "",
        "def enrich(orders, customers, products):",
        "    latest = products.sort_values(\"updated\").drop_duplicates(\"sku\", keep=\"last\")",
        "    m = orders.merge(customers, on=\"customer_id\", how=\"left\", validate=\"many_to_one\")",
        "    m = m.merge(latest[[\"sku\", \"price\"]], on=\"sku\", how=\"left\", validate=\"many_to_one\")",
        "    m[\"revenue\"] = m[\"qty\"] * m[\"price\"]",
        "    return m",
        "",
        "",
        "def month_grid(m):",
        "    g = m.pivot_table(index=\"region\", columns=\"month\", values=\"revenue\", aggfunc=\"sum\", fill_value=0)",
        "    g = g[[\"Jan\", \"Feb\", \"Mar\"]]",
        "    g[\"growth\"] = g[\"Mar\"] - g[\"Jan\"]",
        "    return g"
      ],
      "hints": [
        "`pivot_table(index=\"region\", columns=\"month\", values=\"revenue\", aggfunc=\"sum\", fill_value=0)`",
        "Select the months in order, then add `growth`."
      ],
      "template": [
        "{{CODE}}",
        "",
        "_orders = pd.DataFrame({",
        "    \"order_id\": [1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7, 8],",
        "    \"customer_id\": [10, 20, 10, 30, 20, 10, 40, 30],",
        "    \"sku\": [\"T1\", \"C1\", \"C1\", \"T1\", \"T1\", \"C1\", \"T1\", \"C1\"],",
        "    \"qty\": [2, 1, 3, 1, 4, 1, 2, 2],",
        "    \"month\": [\"Jan\", \"Jan\", \"Feb\", \"Feb\", \"Feb\", \"Mar\", \"Mar\", \"Mar\"],",
        "})",
        "_customers = pd.DataFrame({\"customer_id\": [10, 20, 30, 40], \"region\": [\"North\", \"South\", \"North\", \"East\"]})",
        "_products = pd.DataFrame({\"sku\": [\"T1\", \"C1\", \"T1\"], \"price\": [3.0, 8.0, 3.5],",
        "                          \"updated\": [\"2024-01-01\", \"2024-01-01\", \"2024-06-01\"]})",
        "",
        "_g = month_grid(enrich(_orders, _customers, _products))",
        "Dojo.eq(\"columns\", [\"Jan\", \"Feb\", \"Mar\", \"growth\"], list(_g.columns))",
        "Dojo.eq(\"regions\", [\"East\", \"North\", \"South\"], _g.index.tolist())",
        "Dojo.eq(\"North\", [7.0, 27.5, 24.0, 17.0], [float(v) for v in _g.loc[\"North\"]])",
        "Dojo.eq(\"South\", [8.0, 14.0, 0.0, -8.0], [float(v) for v in _g.loc[\"South\"]])",
        "Dojo.eq(\"East\", [0.0, 0.0, 7.0, 7.0], [float(v) for v in _g.loc[\"East\"]])"
      ]
    }
  ]
